19231      /* STAT-SURVEYFREQ-005: SURVEYFREQ — Jackknife Method
19232       * Source: S154 / Chapter 118 / `Jackknife Method` (PDF pp. 9639–9641).
19233       * Discriminates: Verified default procedure context
19234       */
19235      options nosyntaxcheck obs=max firstobs=1 nodate nonumber nocenter linesize=160 pagesize=max nostimer nofullstimer validvarname=v7
19235    ! validmemname=compatible locale=en_US;
19236      %let syscc=0;
19237      title; footnote;
19238      ods _all_ close;
19239      ods listing gpath="%sysfunc(pathname(work))";
19240      ods graphics off;
19241      proc datasets library=work kill nolist;
NOTE: Deleting WORK.REGSTRY (memtype=ITEMSTOR).
NOTE: File WORK.REGSTRY (memtype=ITEMSTOR) cannot be deleted because it is in use.
NOTE: Deleting WORK.SASGOPT (memtype=CATALOG).
NOTE: File WORK.SASGOPT (memtype=CATALOG) cannot be deleted because it is in use.
NOTE: Deleting WORK.SURVEY (memtype=DATA).
NOTE: Deleting WORK.TEMPLAT (memtype=ITEMSTOR).
NOTE: File WORK.TEMPLAT (memtype=ITEMSTOR) cannot be deleted because it is in use.
19241    !                                         quit;


19242      ods path work.templat(update) sashelp.tmplmst(read);
19243      
19244      data survey;
19245      do state=1 to 2;
19246      do school=1 to 4;
19247      do id=1 to 6;
19248      response=1+mod(id+school,3);
19249      schooltype=1+mod(school,2);
19250      samplingweight=2+state+school/10;
19251      output;
19252      end;
19253      end;
19254      end;
19255      run;

NOTE: The data set WORK.SURVEY has 48 observations and 6 variables.

19256      proc surveyfreq data=survey;
19257      strata state;
19258      cluster school;
19259      weight samplingweight;
19260      tables schooltype*response / row chisq;
19261      run;

NOTE: The Rao-Scott chi-square test cannot be computed for the table of schooltype by response because the design correction is not positive.
NOTE: The PROCEDURE SURVEYFREQ printed page 1381.

